  "content_en": "The Great Han Yanhua Quotation Ⅰ Zhuang Zhou’s Nth revision strives to make the introduction chapter less literary. I think I’d better explain that the two chapters in the introduction volume tell the modern story before Zhang Yan’s time travel. Comrades who don’t like the past time travel can skip it. Start directly from the first volume. The main text is in the third person, but in the quotation, the first person is used for emotional portrayal. The ancient sage Zhuang Zhou dreamed that he had become a butterfly. When he woke up, he was suddenly confused. He did not know whether he was the Zhuang Zhou who dreamed of a butterfly or the butterfly in Zhuang Zhou's dream. Two thousand years later, I am lingering on the line between dreams and reality. When I listen to the story of Zhuang Zhou dreaming of a butterfly again, I feel something in my heart. I can no longer tell whether I am Zhuang Zhou in the dream or the butterfly who is awake. In 2000, Wan'er transferred his job to Xi'an, and at the same time I was admitted to the Agricultural College of a local university. Wan'er said, \"There will be very few opportunities to return to Handan in the future. Let's go to the cemetery to pay homage to my parents.\" Wan'er is my brother. I was little more than a teenager when our parents died in a plane crash. At the memorial service, my aunt stretched out her hand to us and said, \"Wan'er, Yanran, come home with me.\" Wan'er stood in front of me and shouted hoarsely, \"Don't worry about us, I will take care of Yanran.\" I hugged the broken doll and hid behind Wan'er shivering. When I looked up, I saw that the figure of my brother standing in front of me was very tall, just like the father who used to protect us from the wind and rain. Wan'er said, \"I'm sorry, Yanran. Brother can't cook well. You deal with it first. Tomorrow I will learn to cook the food well, just like my mother before.\" Wan'er said, \"If you want to bully my sister, you have to beat me to death first.\" Wan'er pulled me to grow up. The customs of Handan have the flavor of my hometown. I bought a large bouquet of cornflowers. I can no longer remember what my parents looked like, but I still remember with a smile, he stroked the tall and white tombstone and said, \"Mom and Dad, I have finally brought Yanran up. You should be able to rest assured.\" A few tears fell. I placed the cornflowers in front of the tombstone and smiled and said, \"Let's go.\" When we left the cemetery gate, we met an old woman. As we passed each other, she opened her mouth and called out, \"...Yan.\" I turned around in shock and asked, \"Mother-in-law, are you calling me?\" She nodded, with a slight coldness and hatred in her eyes, \"...it's about to start. Are you ready?\" I was at a loss, \"Mother-in-law, what are you talking about?\" \"You will understand in the future.\" She smiled, \"When you really understand, I hope you can still be this happy. My name is...\" Wan You dragged me forward, \"Let's go, let's go.\" He frowned in disgust, \"Why do you care about such a bastard?\" \"Hey--\" I couldn't stop, so I had to turn back while walking with a smile. I didn't hear my grandma's words clearly, so I waved and shouted, \"Grandma, I'm sorry-\" Moving is a very tiring thing. I turned around and said goodbye to my hometown, my hometown, step by step. My mood was as depressed as the continuous rain. It is a heart-wrenching pain to say goodbye to a period of your life completely. \"But it's also the beginning of a new life.\" Wan'er comforted, \"So don't look back, so you can see ahead. Don't just remember to be sad, remember to be happy.\" At an altitude of tens of thousands of feet, I turned to look at my brother and promised him, \"Okay.\" I started to have a dream. In the dream, there are stretches of pavilions and wide-angle cornices. The slaves came in and out in a hurry, bringing out basin after basin of blood. In the side room, the woman's painful cry of childbirth was loud and helpless. The middle-aged servant woman hurriedly walked out and knelt in front of the man with a tall hat and a belt. Then the man closed his eyes. He hesitated for a while and seemed to make a decision, but his face looked painful. There was a faint color of blood, and time passed by like an hourglass. Among the heavy curtains, the haggard woman opened her eyes amidst the blood. She was gentle but firm. The servant woman persuaded her earnestly, but the woman remained the same. Outside, an old man with cloudy eyes walked up to the man and said something. The man frowned and hesitated for a long time, shed a few tears, and finally nodded. It seemed that after a very short and very long time, the sound of a baby crying finally penetrated the dawn sky. The scene suddenly changed, and the man came to the side hall with the child in his arms. In the side hall, the female fortune teller turned her head and smiled in the direction of nothingness. In the dream, I was horrified. The female fortune teller standing there with her hands behind her hands could slowly turn into the old woman I met by chance in the Handan Cemetery if her figure had declined a little more, her hair had turned gray, and her eyes had lines. What's going on? in dreamI was horrified. The new father bowed slightly to the female fortune teller. The female physiognomist took the baby from his hands and giggled when she saw the swaddled baby, which was still slightly pink, opened its eyes. \"Congratulations to the crown prince,\" the female fortune teller opened her mouth and enunciated the words clearly, \"The little prince has a very precious fortune, and he will definitely become a great person in the future.\" Each word was deafening, as if thunder was ringing in my ears, each sound louder than the last. She said, \"This woman's fortune is extremely precious.\" \"——Extremely expensive.\"...\"Yanran, Yanran——\" The smiling voice rang in my ears. I woke up from my dream, opened my eyes, and saw my brother standing beside the bed in the bright light. I exhaled and threw myself into his arms in my pajamas, \"Smile, I had a strange dream.\" \"What's so strange about dreaming?\" Smiled disapprovingly, \"I'm up, the sun is shining on my butt.\" There is nothing strange about dreaming, but this dream was so clear and real that I could remember every fold of the clothes of the person in the dream. And the female fortune teller I met in Handan Cemetery. In September, Wan'er sent me to school. On campus, Luo Mi stopped me dragging my luggage and asked, \"Classmate, do you know how to get to the dormitory building?\" She was wearing a red windbreaker, wavy curly hair, slightly twitching her eyes, and a bright smile. She became my roommate. Later, she hugged my shoulders and said, \"There are so many people on campus, but I only stopped you. It's fate.\" I said, \"Nie fate, oh fate.\" It's fate. Luo Mi's hometown is Inner Mongolia. It is said that she has the blood of grassland ethnic minorities, a kind of bold and unrestrained beauty. She said that she could ride a horse across the grassland all day and night, so she couldn't stand the weakness of the inland people. \"Maybe my ancestors have the blood of the Golden Family,\" she said dreamily when introducing herself. \"I am Luo Mi, a mechanical major. Luofu Luo, Mi Tang Ni.\" She smiled and stretched out her hand with beautiful fingers. I also smiled, stretched out my hand, and said, \"My name is Zhang Yanran, the smiling Yanran.\" Zhang Yanran likes this girl named Luo Mi, in this life, in the past life, in the next life, in the next life, in the three lives. That night, I had my second dream. The train of her skirt dragged over the stone steps, and the woman with three buns and six hairpins walked down holding the slave's hand. She stopped a dozen feet away from the high platform and looked up at her husband. He was standing in front of the solemn ancestral temple, wearing a crown, clear and dignified. In front of him, the servant woman stood holding a baby girl. The man bent down and took the baby girl's right hand. Then the baby girl babbled and laughed, her laughter clear and clear. The woman lowered her eyes and listened to her husband's solemn voice coming from her word by word: \"...I have a daughter today, Huimin is well-qualified, and she is worthy of being an example...named: Yan.\" I woke up from the dream, gasping for air, like a frightened fish in a dry pond. I said to myself, this is just a simple dream. But he is so weak that he cannot even convince himself. The man who named my daughter in the dream was clearly the same man as the man in my last dream. I seem to have watched a pantomime in my dream. I don’t know who directed it, who edited it, and who appeared on stage. The plot is consistent and the characters and scenes are grand. There were so many people performing, but there was only one person watching the show, and there was no need to spend money on tickets. A treat that is too grand will only make people feel uneasy. \"Yanran, what's wrong?\" Luo Mi poked her head out from the mosquito net of the bed opposite and called softly. I calmed down and said softly, \"It's okay, I just had a dream.\" In the dark night, Luo Mi's big eyes sparkled in surprise, and she said, \"What a coincidence, I also had a dream.\" \"I started dreaming a month before I came to Xi'an. See the grand grassland. Yanran, don’t laugh. Although I grew up in the grassland, I have never seen such a beautiful grassland. The green grass grows to half a person’s height. The man in leather clothes rides a strong horse. That’s called a real strong horse. , Real men, spat, today’s men have a kind of cream in their bones.” “I dreamed that a woman gave birth to a child in a big felt tent, and people milked the cow and fed the child. At night, the felt tent lit up. People sang loudly around the bonfire, and the big man with his hair and animal skin clothes laughed and held his child while drinking. \"This is the real grassland.\" Luo Mi yearned for it infinitely. I invited Luo Mi to my home as a guest, and we got acquainted with Wan Er. After coming to Xi'an, Wan'er's craftsmanship became more and more sophisticated, and she was full of praise for the chicken, rice, bean sprouts and romaine. I teased her, \"I like chicken rice sprouts so much.\"Food, why don't you marry my brother and you can eat it every day. Luo Mi raised her head slightly and said proudly, \"Am I, Luo Mi, worth a bowl of chicken, rice and sprouts?\" \"The autumn wind blew the fallen leaves, and I saw the broad sky and the palace city located under the sky. The woman from the previous episode got off the carriage and walked into the palace with Yan in her arms. A woman in gorgeous clothes and a high bun came up to her and cried bitterly while hugging the visitor. The years left traces on her face, her skin became old and her complexion faded. The only thing worth mentioning is What was praised was her majesty, her long eyebrows raised at the temples, resolute and strong. The two cried bitterly for a while, then rejoiced. She took Yan from the woman's arms and coaxed her lovingly, \"Manhua,\" she raised her head and said solemnly, \"Mom has nothing left, only you and Ying'er are left. \"Mom will risk her life to keep what you deserve for you.\" \"When I woke up from the dream again, I could already feel calm. Luo Mi said, \"What can we do besides just watching the fun? \"How is it? How is it? I don't know what will happen. I want to find out the meaning of these dreams. In the winter vacation, Luo Mi returned to her hometown on the grassland, and I also went home to celebrate the New Year. \"I have been very unlucky recently,\" smiled and complained to me about the new strict manager. I responded humbly, holding a bowl and drinking from him. I made yam and chicken soup, which made me feel very homely and warm. I started going in and out of the library to look up the architectural styles I had seen in my dreams and the clothes of the people in my dreams. When I took down the \"Chinese Clothing Illustration\" on the upper shelf, I saw \"Ammi.\" \"I called her. \"Hey, Yanran? \"Luo Mi turned around, holding a book in her hand. I caught a glimpse of the title: \"History of the Prairie Minorities.\" We all laughed. There was a tacit understanding in our hearts. \"Have you found anything? she asked me. \"Hmm.\" \"I nodded, \"I have looked up the history of Chinese architecture before, and the building I saw in my dream was a high-rise building that appeared from the Pre-Qin period to the Han Dynasty. After the middle of the Western Han Dynasty, high platform buildings were gradually abandoned. \"Hey,\" I said in frustration, holding the book again, \"So what if we really find out?\" The dreams that should be dreamed will continue to be dreamed. Nothing will change. Luo Mi smiled mysteriously, \"At least you'll understand better when you watch the show.\" \"We giggled. It is our unique drama. The new book is online,",
